pk_wide.c, pk_wide.h, pk_wide_games.h, pk_cheats.h and pk_coop_emerald.h imported from commit
0040e61fcb129d7313e3941771572c93d6722816 (ZOOM and the look-around for the GBA games). FullDex's changes:
pk_wide.c's two mGBA names (GBA_SIZE_EWRAM, GBA_BASE_PALETTE_RAM) for the newer mGBA and Windows' far / near
macros undone, the field's 512-wide BGs (FullDex's widescreen patches) read in its tilemap check, built with
PK_WIDE_NO_GUARD; pk_wide_gb_none.c stands in for the Game Boy half (FullDex plays no Game Boy games).

pk_flight.c, pk_flight.h and pk_flight_vehicles.h (FREE FLIGHT) imported from the same commit, unchanged; their
addresses for the English retail games are generated into ../flight_records.h by tools/gen_flight.py from PokeDaisy's
GameDataRecordsGen.kt. pk_call_lite.c also carries pk_call.c's between-frames call (pk_game_call) for FLY.
pk_wide.c's FREE FLIGHT glide (flyGlide) keeps going through a map crossing's held frames (ten frames without a
view, not two) and restarts at the flight's speed; pk_flight.c gained FLY ON a Pokemon (pk_flight_set_mount).
